Section 13: running it over a network

CircleSong is a web application, so most people will use it without ever
downloading it. Section 13 of the AGPL exists for exactly that case: anyone
interacting with this program remotely over a network must be offered the
corresponding source of the version they are using.

The app satisfies this with a "Source Code (AGPL v3.0)" link in its About
panel and in its footer, both pointing at the repository above. If you deploy
a modified copy, that link must point at *your* modified source.

This notice used to live at the top of LICENSE. It was moved here so that
LICENSE is the verbatim text of the GNU AGPL v3 and licence detectors can
recognise it; nothing about the terms changed.
